---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import data from '../data/providers.json';
import Status from '../components/Status.astro';
import { STATUS_TEXT, CHECKED_ON, PICK_RULE, countryPick, u } from '../site.js';
import Byline from '../components/Byline.astro';
import { allCountries } from '../lib/countries.js';
const picks = allCountries().map((c) => ({ c, pk: countryPick(c.slug) })).filter((x) => x.pk);
const noPick = allCountries().filter((c) => !countryPick(c.slug));
---
<Base title="How we pick and check provider facts" description="How Get Paid From Anywhere picks one payment provider per country, where every fact comes from, what each status answer means, and how corrections work." crumb="How we pick">
  <div class="prose">
  <h1>How we pick</h1>
  <Byline date={CHECKED_ON} />
  <p class="lede">Each country page names one provider to start with. The pick comes from a fixed rule applied to facts on the providers' own pages, so you can check it yourself.</p>

  <h2 id="rule">The rule</h2>
  <ol>{PICK_RULE.map((r) => <li>{r}</li>)}</ol>
  <p>The base fee is the first percent plus cents fee on the provider's pricing page, before extra fees for international cards, subscriptions or payout methods. Each pick shows those extra fees next to it.</p>

  <h2 id="picks">Today's picks</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Country</th><th>Pick</th><th>Base fee</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{picks.map(({ c, pk }) => <tr><th scope="row"><a href={u(`/country/${c.slug}/`)}>{c.name}</a></th><td><a href={u(`/provider/${pk.p.slug}/`)}>{pk.p.name}</a></td><td class="num">{pk.fee?.text}</td><td>{pk.named ? 'Names the country on its own list' : 'Country is not on its banned list'}{pk.tie ? ', ties on fee and publishes all extra fees' : ''}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  {noPick.length > 0 && <p><small>No pick yet for {noPick.map((c) => c.name).join(', ')}. We have not yet recorded each merchant of record's status there in the dataset, so those pages answer in plain text.</small></p>}

  <h2 id="sources">Where facts come from</h2>
  <p>Every fact comes from the provider's own website: help center, documentation, pricing or legal pages. We do not use reviews, forum posts or third-party blogs as a source. Each fact in the <a href={u('/data/providers.json')}>dataset</a> carries its source link and the date we checked it. The current data was checked on {CHECKED_ON}.</p>

  <h2 id="labels">What each answer means</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Answer</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{Object.entries(data.statusLegend).map(([k, v]) => <tr><td><Status status={k} /></td><td>{v}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>"{STATUS_TEXT['not-excluded']}" is weaker than "{STATUS_TEXT['listed']}". Some providers, such as Paddle and Wise, publish a list of countries they cannot serve instead of a list they can. A country missing from that list is not a promise of approval.</p>
  <p>"{STATUS_TEXT['unknown']}" means we could not confirm it on the provider's own site. It does not mean no. Ask the provider.</p>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not publish user reviews, star ratings or traffic numbers.</li>
    <li>We do not rank providers by affiliate payout.</li>
    <li>We do not give legal, tax or financial advice. Forming a US company or receiving foreign payments can have tax and regulatory consequences in your country.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Updates and corrections</h2>
  <p>When we recheck a provider page, we update the checked date. If a provider page changes and a fact here is wrong, we fix it and note the new date. To report an error, see the <a href={u('/about/')}>About</a> page. Affiliate relationships never change facts, answers or picks. Read the <a href={u('/affiliate-disclosure/')}>affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
